---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Base title="Research projects" description="Generation trajectory evidence and our next-frequency research, presented as separate reports.">
  <div class="home-shell shell">
    <section class="home-hero">
      <p class="section-overline">Research collection / two reports</p>
      <h1>How images <em>take shape.</em></h1>
      <p>Explore generation trajectories across released models, then inspect our next-frequency method, samples and matched experiments in its own report.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#projects">Explore the reports <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </section>
    <section id="projects" class="home-projects">
      <div class="home-section-top"><h2>Reports</h2><span>02 / generation research</span></div>
      <article class="home-feature">
        <a class="home-feature-visual" href={withBase('projects/generation-step-by-step/')} aria-label="Open the streaming trajectory report"><img src={withBase('report/img/ffhq128_mid_x0.jpg')} alt="DCTdiff FFHQ-128 generation progression across sampling calls" loading="lazy" /><span>Streaming trajectory audit / 21 public runs + ours A1</span></a>
        <div class="home-feature-copy"><p class="section-overline">01 / Comparative audit</p><h3><a href={withBase('projects/generation-step-by-step/')}>Generation, Step by Step</a></h3><p>Follow eight fixed samples per run. Our A1 FFHQ-64 progression now sits alongside DCTdiff, FAR and other released models in the same figure rail, graph and trajectory viewer.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('projects/generation-step-by-step/')}>Explore trajectories <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="home-feature">
        <a class="home-feature-visual" href={withBase('projects/next-frequency/')} aria-label="Open our next-frequency report"><img src={withBase('ours/ffhq64-a1-d256/a1-grid-146k.png')} alt="A1 D256 FFHQ-64 generated sample grid at 146k steps" loading="lazy" /><span>Our method / A1 next-frequency</span></a>
        <div class="home-feature-copy"><p class="section-overline">02 / Our method</p><h3><a href={withBase('projects/next-frequency/')}>Next-frequency generation</a></h3><p>The four-stage generator, its saved FFHQ-64 samples, matched-compute evaluation, and the separate CIFAR-10 STRONG result with its G2 checkerboard caveat.</p><div class="home-result"><strong>≈5%</strong><span>CIFAR-10 D192 · relative FID cost at matched 100k<br />pre-registered STRONG criterion met</span></div><a class="text-link" href={withBase('projects/next-frequency/')}>Read our report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </section>
    <p class="home-footnote">The CIFAR-10 and FFHQ-64 results use different models and protocols. Each report labels evidence sources and limits where its results appear.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
